   "start": 58.467,
   "duration": 18.65,
   "end": 77.117,
   "text": "To see why, take one eruption two minutes long. The data's curve stands this high there: call it p. [pause 0.45] The bell gives it q, [pause 0.3] about a quarter as much. Double q twice and you reach p. [pause 0.45] So log base two of p over q is about two: two doublings, or two bits.",
